1
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Starring in Her First Movie!

2
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Barbie in the Nutcracker is a animation, family film directed by Owen Hurley.

3
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:39,000
The Mouse King casts an evil spell over Clara that causes her to shrink.

4
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Clara and the Nutcracker set out on an adventurous journey to find
Sugarplum Princess, who has the power to undo the spell.

5
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Barbie / Clara (voice), played by Kelly Sheridan.

6
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Nutcracker / Prince Eric (voice), played by Kirby Morrow.

7
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:03,000
Mouse King (voice), played by Tim Curry.

8
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Pimm (voice), played by Peter Kelamis.

9
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Major Mint (voice), played by Christopher Gaze.

10
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Captain Candy (voice), played by Ian James Corlett.

11
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Barbie in the Nutcracker is a 2001 animated fantasy film co-produced by Mainframe
Entertainment and Mattel Entertainment, and distributed by Artisan Home Entertainment.

12
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Loosely adapted from E.

13
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Hoffmann's 1816 short story, "The Nutcracker and the Mouse King", and featuring music based from Tchaikovsky's 1892 ballet, The Nutcracker, it marked the character's first film since the
1987 television specials; Barbie and the Rockers: Out of This World and Barbie and the Sensations: Rockin' Back to Earth, with Kelly Sheridan providing the voice of Barbie.

14
00:53:54,000 --> 00:54:00,000
It was also the first Barbie movie to be computer-animated.

15
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Barbie in the Nutcracker premiered on VHS on October 2, 2001, by Artisan,
followed up with a DVD release a few weeks later on October 23.

16
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
before being subsequently released overseas through
Entertainment Rights and Universal Pictures Video.

17
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:33,000
The film sold more than 3.4 million units on DVD by 2002,
and grossed $150 million in total sales.

18
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
It won the Video Premiere Award for Best Animated Video Premiere Movie.

19
01:13:09,000 --> 01:13:15,000
The film explores themes of magic, mouse, musical, ballet, based on toy.
